-- §67(א), (ד) as replaced: the pay changes on a change in the school itself
-- (not one caused by other schools alone), and on the principal's move to a
-- school of another level. A change caused by other schools changes nothing
-- for the principal in office; the next principal is paid by the level on
-- his entry.
@ref akn:art_46/p1
GIVEN `the change comes from the school itself` IS A BOOLEAN, `the principal moved to a school of another level` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a change of level changes the principal's pay` `the change comes from the school itself` `the principal moved to a school of another level` IF
    `the change comes from the school itself` OR `the principal moved to a school of another level`

-- (ב): on a rise, the combined salary of the new level, as before.
GIVEN `the new level's combined salary` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the principal's combined salary after a rise, as §67 is replaced` `the new level's combined salary` IS
    `the principal's combined salary after a rise` `the new level's combined salary`

-- (ג)(1)–(4): on a fall, beside the table pay, the "accumulated complexity
-- supplement" N: M − the value of the new level, M being the banked 10% of
-- each year's level value (the value being the principal's combined salary
-- less a level-1 principal's of his grade) plus [100% − 10% × his years] ×
-- the new level's value — the base agreement's sum (§67(ד) there), which
-- F-ofek-hadash-base-67-a reads with the years counted to ten.
-- F-ofek-hadash-hashlama-2012-c: the clause that replaces §67 caps the years at ten
-- only for a further fall ((ג)(6)); the first fall's (3) runs past ten as
-- the base agreement's did. The reading adopted is that finding's.
GIVEN `level value in each year so far` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      `the new level's value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the accumulated complexity supplement` `level value in each year so far` `the new level's value` IS
    `not below zero` (`the supplement after a fall` `level value in each year so far` `the new level's value` MINUS `the new level's value`)

GIVEN `level value in each year so far` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      `the new level's value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the accumulated complexity supplement, as printed` `level value in each year so far` `the new level's value` IS
    `the supplement after a fall, as printed` `level value in each year so far` `the new level's value` MINUS `the new level's value`

-- The base agreement's example of four years at level 3 and a fall to
-- level 2: M is 1,705.2, so N is 487.2 beside the level-2 table pay.
#ASSERT `the accumulated complexity supplement` `four years at level 3` 1218 EQUALS 487.2
#ASSERT `the complexity supplement` 20000 17564 EQUALS 2436

-- F-ofek-hadash-hashlama-2012-c's evidence: twelve years at level 3, then a first fall
-- to level 2 — as printed, N is more than the whole level-3 value.
`after twelve years a first fall still raises the supplement under the replaced §67` MEANS
    `the accumulated complexity supplement, as printed` `twelve years at level 3` 1218 PLUS 1218 GREATER THAN 2436
#ASSERT `after twelve years a first fall still raises the supplement under the replaced §67`

-- (ג)(5): a later rise — of the school's level, or a move to a higher one —
-- takes N down by the rise in his pay, to nothing at most.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the rise in his pay` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the accumulated complexity supplement after a rise` n `the rise in his pay` IS
    `not below zero` (n MINUS `the rise in his pay`)

#ASSERT `the accumulated complexity supplement after a rise` 487.2 1218 EQUALS 0

-- (ג)(6): a further fall, or a move to a lower level, recomputes N, with
-- the level values of (up to) his first ten years as principal on the
-- reform's terms.
GIVEN `level value in each year so far` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      `the new level's value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the accumulated complexity supplement after a further fall` `level value in each year so far` `the new level's value` IS
    `the accumulated complexity supplement` (take 10 `level value in each year so far`) `the new level's value`

