-- (ג): §134 as replaced: age hours off the position base — an existing
-- kindergarten teacher of 50 to 55 (not 55), 2 a week; of 55 and up, 4; a
-- new one of 50 and up, 2, and no more at 55. (ד): by her age on 31
-- December of the school year, from the year's start.
@ref akn:art_75__para_c
GIVEN `an existing kindergarten teacher` IS A BOOLEAN, `age on 31 December of the school year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a kindergarten teacher's age-hours reduction` `an existing kindergarten teacher` `age on 31 December of the school year` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `age on 31 December of the school year` LESS THAN 50 THEN 0
        IF `an existing kindergarten teacher` AND `age on 31 December of the school year` AT LEAST 55 THEN 4
        OTHERWISE 2

#ASSERT `a kindergarten teacher's age-hours reduction` TRUE 55 EQUALS 4
#ASSERT `a kindergarten teacher's age-hours reduction` FALSE 60 EQUALS 2

-- (ד): §134א: (א) her position is her weekly hours over her position base;
-- (ב) §27(א)–(ו) apply to part time; (ג) §33(א) (the 100% cap) and §33(ב)
-- do not apply to her, but her weekly hours are 42 at most; (ד) above 100%,
-- §33(ד)(3)–(4) apply. No rounding is stated (convention rounding.default).
@ref akn:art_75__para_d
GIVEN `weekly hours` IS A NUMBER, p IS A `kindergarten teacher's charge`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `a kindergarten teacher's position` `weekly hours` p IS
    IF `weekly hours` GREATER THAN 42
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`weekly hours` DIVIDED BY `a kindergarten teacher's position base` p)

#ASSERT `a kindergarten teacher's position` 33.8 `a complementing kindergarten teacher` EQUALS JUST 1
#ASSERT `a kindergarten teacher's position` 43 `a complementing kindergarten teacher` EQUALS NOTHING

