@ref akn:art_90
GIVEN p IS A `population §155(ב) leaves to negotiation`, `the reform has been applied to it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `§§88 and 89 apply to the population` p `the reform has been applied to it` IF
    `the reform has been applied to it`

§§ `91 ביטול בדיקות השחיקה`

-- (א): from the signing, every provision of the collective agreements on
-- the erosion of teachers' pay against engineers' pay — the checks and the
-- compensation — is cancelled. (ב): for every teaching employee in the
-- civil service, notwithstanding §3. §153(ב) of the base agreement had
-- already taken reform employment out of the comparison.
@ref akn:art_91__para_a akn:art_91__para_b
GIVEN `the employment is under the reform` IS A BOOLEAN, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the erosion comparison applies on` `the employment is under the reform` d IF
        `the erosion comparison applies to the employment` `the employment is under the reform`
    AND NOT d `is on or after` `the signing of the completion agreement`

#ASSERT `the erosion comparison applies on` FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 28 2 2012)
#ASSERT NOT `the erosion comparison applies on` FALSE `the signing of the completion agreement`

§§ `92 יישום עלות הסכם המסגרת והפחתת עלות להקצאה עתידית`

-- ¶1: following the negotiation of §155(א) of the base agreement, and to
-- fund what this agreement changes (§§88–89 among them), the allocations of
-- the framework agreement of 12.1.2011 (as amended on 11.4.2011) due from
-- 1.1.2012, 1.1.2013 and 1.7.2013 are made as follows.
@ref akn:art_92/p1
`the days the framework allocations were due` MEANS LIST DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2012, DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2013, DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2013

-- akn:art_92__para_a The lead-in to (א): the allocation from January 2012.

-- (א)(1): from 1.1.2012 the salary tables of teaching employees on the
-- reform's terms, and of those in supervision and staff roles under the
-- agreement of 5.7.2010, are updated so that their total update over the
-- tables in force before the update of 1.1.2011 (agreement of 25.1.2011) is
-- 4%. ¶2–¶3: the updated tables are annexed (annexes 1'–22' and 1'–8'), not
-- in the corpus; an input.
@ref akn:art_92__para_a__subpara_1 akn:art_92__para_a__subpara_1/p2 akn:art_92__para_a__subpara_1/p3
`the total update of the reform tables from 1.1.2012` MEANS 4%

ASSUME `the updated reform tables of 1.1.2012` IS A FUNCTION FROM NUMBER AND NUMBER TO NUMBER

GIVEN `a cell before the update of 1.1.2011` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a reform table cell from 1.1.2012, by the total update` `a cell before the update of 1.1.2011` IS
    `a cell before the update of 1.1.2011` `increased by` `the total update of the reform tables from 1.1.2012`

#ASSERT `a reform table cell from 1.1.2012, by the total update` 10000 EQUALS 10400

-- (א)(2): for teaching employees off the reform (not in supervision and
-- staff roles): (א) the 2011 supplement is paid at 4% from 1.1.2012; (ב)
-- the shekel supplements are updated from 1.1.2012 to a total of 4% over
-- their sums before the update of 1.1.2011.
-- (ב): the allocation due in January 2013 is put off three months, to April
-- 2013, and cut by 0.5% (against the rate of §5.1.3 of the framework
-- agreement), so that it completes the rate to 5.75%. (ג): the allocation
-- due in July 2013 is cut by 0.4% (against "the rate of §5.1.3"), so that
-- it completes the rate to 6.35%. (ב) and (ג) do not name what the rate is
-- of; the encoding reads it as (א)(2)(א) names the January 2012 one, the
-- 2011 supplement's — the rate later circulars cite as "the rate set under
-- §92(ג)" when they raise the 2011 supplement to 6.35%.
-- F-ofek-hadash-hashlama-2012-g: the two cuts are measured against one
-- clause and cannot both be; the printed rates govern. Before 1.1.2012 the
-- 2011 supplement is the agreement of 25.1.2011's, an input.
@ref akn:art_92__para_a__subpara_2 akn:art_92__para_a__subpara_2__cls_a akn:art_92__para_b akn:art_92__para_c
`1 January 2012` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2012
`1 April 2013` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 2013
`1 July 2013` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2013

`the 2011 supplement rate from 1 January 2012` MEANS 4%
`the 2011 supplement rate from 1 April 2013` MEANS 5.75%
-- §92(ג)'s rate.
`the 2011 supplement rate from 1 July 2013` MEANS 6.35%
`the cut of the January 2013 allocation` MEANS 0.5%
`the cut of the July 2013 allocation` MEANS 0.4%
`the January 2013 allocation is made from` MEANS `1 April 2013`

GIVEN `the rate before 1.1.2012` IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 2011 supplement rate under §92` `the rate before 1.1.2012` d IS
    BRANCH
        IF d `is on or after` `1 July 2013` THEN `the 2011 supplement rate from 1 July 2013`
        IF d `is on or after` `the January 2013 allocation is made from` THEN `the 2011 supplement rate from 1 April 2013`
        IF d `is on or after` `1 January 2012` THEN `the 2011 supplement rate from 1 January 2012`
        OTHERWISE `the rate before 1.1.2012`

#ASSERT `the 2011 supplement rate under §92` (2.5%) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 2 2013) EQUALS 4%
#ASSERT `the 2011 supplement rate under §92` (2.5%) `1 April 2013` EQUALS 5.75%
#ASSERT `the 2011 supplement rate under §92` (2.5%) `1 July 2013` EQUALS 6.35%
#ASSERT `the 2011 supplement rate under §92` (2.5%) (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 2011) EQUALS 2.5%

@ref akn:art_92__para_a__subpara_2__cls_b
GIVEN `a shekel supplement before the update of 1.1.2011` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a shekel supplement from 1.1.2012` `a shekel supplement before the update of 1.1.2011` IS
    `a shekel supplement before the update of 1.1.2011` `increased by` `the 2011 supplement rate from 1 January 2012`

-- F-ofek-hadash-hashlama-2012-g's evidence: each cut is measured "against
-- the rate of §5.1.3", and the rate it leaves plus the cut is the rate it
-- was cut from — 6.25% for (ב) and 6.75% for (ג), two rates for one clause;
-- and §94(ב) places the July 2013 part, the fourth, in §5.1.4.
`the §5.1.3 rate (ב) implies` MEANS `the 2011 supplement rate from 1 April 2013` PLUS `the cut of the January 2013 allocation`
`the §5.1.3 rate (ג) implies` MEANS `the 2011 supplement rate from 1 July 2013` PLUS `the cut of the July 2013 allocation`
`the framework clause §92(ג) measures the July 2013 cut against` MEANS "5.1.3"
`the framework clause §94(ב) gives the fourth part` MEANS "5.1.4"
`§92(ב) and (ג) measure against one clause two different rates` MEANS
        (NOT `the §5.1.3 rate (ב) implies` EQUALS `the §5.1.3 rate (ג) implies`)
    AND (NOT `the framework clause §92(ג) measures the July 2013 cut against` EQUALS `the framework clause §94(ב) gives the fourth part`)
#ASSERT `§92(ב) and (ג) measure against one clause two different rates`

-- (ד): §92 reaches every teaching employee in the civil service,
-- notwithstanding §3 (see `covered by §§91 and 92`).
@ref akn:art_92__para_d
`§92 reaches a teaching employee outside §3's workplaces` MEANS
    `covered by §§91 and 92` (`employee under the completion agreement` WITH `ranked on the teaching employees' scale` IS TRUE, `in the civil service` IS TRUE, workplace IS `another workplace`)
#ASSERT `§92 reaches a teaching employee outside §3's workplaces`

§ `ד. תיקון תשלומי יתר במסגרת יישום הרפורמה`

§§ `93 ניכוי תשלומי יתר שבוצעו בעקבות המרות שכר`

-- (א): an overpayment made by a mistake in a conversion is an advance on
-- wages for §25(א)(7) of the Wage Protection Law, 1958 — so it may be
-- deducted. (ב): the employee is told in writing, about a month before the
-- deduction starts, of the mistake. (ג): it is deducted in equal parts from
-- twelve monthly salaries. (ד): the union says this admits no mistake in
-- anyone's pay. (ה): the clause lapses on 31.8.2014.
@ref akn:art_93__para_a akn:art_93__para_c
`months an overpayment is deducted over` MEANS 12

GIVEN overpayment IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the monthly deduction of a conversion overpayment` overpayment IS
    overpayment DIVIDED BY `months an overpayment is deducted over`

#ASSERT `the monthly deduction of a conversion overpayment` 1200 EQUALS 100

`a conversion overpayment is an advance on wages` MEANS TRUE

-- (ב): written notice of the mistake about a month ("כחודש") before the
-- deduction starts. The duty is the notice; the time is stated loosely and
-- the encoding sets no count of days on it.
@ref akn:art_93__para_b
`notifying the overpayment` MEANS
    PARTY `the State`
    MUST  `send written notice of the overpayment a month before the deduction`

@ref akn:art_93__para_d
`§93 admits a mistake in a teacher's pay` MEANS FALSE

@ref akn:art_93__para_e
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `§93 is in force on` d IF
    d `is on or before` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 8 2014)

#ASSERT NOT `§93 is in force on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2014)

§ `ה. מיצוי תביעות`

§§ `94 מיצוי תביעות`

-- (א): the agreement exhausts every claim on the matters it settles; no
-- further negotiation on them; and it exhausts every claim to compensation
-- for the erosion of teachers' pay against engineers', for the past and the
-- future.
@ref akn:art_94__para_a
`no further negotiation on what the agreement settles` MEANS
    (PARTY `the State`
     SHANT `negotiate further on a matter this agreement settles`)
    RAND
    (PARTY `the teachers' union`
     SHANT `negotiate further on a matter this agreement settles`)

`no erosion claim` MEANS
    PARTY `the teachers' union`
    SHANT `raise a claim on the erosion of teachers' pay against engineers' pay`

-- (ב): §92 exhausts §155(א) of the base agreement as to the framework's
-- second part (its §5.1.2) and the rates and days of its third and fourth
-- parts (§§5.1.3 and 5.1.4).
@ref akn:art_94__para_b
`the framework parts §92 exhausts` MEANS LIST "5.1.2", "5.1.3", "5.1.4"

-- F-ofek-hadash-hashlama-2012-h's evidence: the annex numbers at the seven
-- places that leave one blank — §§11(ד), 17(ב), 23(ב) (twice), 40(א) and
-- 51 (twice) — as printed.
`the annex numbers printed at the blanks` MEANS
    LIST "______", "______", "______", "______", "______", "______", "______"
`seven annex numbers are left blank` MEANS
        count `the annex numbers printed at the blanks` EQUALS 7
    AND all (GIVEN n YIELD n EQUALS "______") `the annex numbers printed at the blanks`
#ASSERT `seven annex numbers are left blank`

-- akn:conclusions The sign-off: a label row with no text of its own.
-- akn:conclusions/p1 The signing formula; no rule.
-- akn:conclusions/p2 The signatures; no rule.
-- akn:conclusions/t1 The signatories' sides; no rule.
-- akn:conclusions/p3 The wages commissioner's file number; no rule.
